==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*keusaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ǵews-||taste, choose}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|kiāsa|lang=ofs}} (West Frisian {{term|kieze|lang=fy}}), Old Saxon {{term|kiosan|lang=osx}} (Low German {{term|kesen|lang=nds}}), Dutch {{term|kiezen|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|kiosan|lang=goh}}, {{term|chiosan|lang=goh}} (German {{term|kiesen|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|kjósa|lang=non}} (Danish {{term|kyse|lang=da}}, Icelandic {{term|kjósa|lang=is}}), Gothic {{term|𐌺𐌹𐌿𐍃𐌰𐌽|tr=kiusan|lang=got}}.  The Indo-European root was also the source of Latin {{term|gustus||taste|lang=la}}, Albanian {{term|desha||chosen|lang=sq}}.

